        "@id": "treasury-laws-amendment-australian-consumer-law-review-act-2018.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "treasury-laws-amendment-australian-consumer-law-review-act-2018.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, subsection (1)(a) does not apply if the consignee\nof the goods is not carrying on or engaged in a business, trade,\nprofession or occupation in relation to the goods.\nNote:\nThis subsection was inserted as a response to the decision of the High\nCourt of Australia in Wallis v Downard-Pickford (North Queensland)\nPty Ltd [1994] HCA 17.\n\nConsumer protection  Schedule 10\n\nNo. 132, 2018\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Australian Consumer Law Review) Act",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, subsection (1)(a) does not apply if the consignee\nof the goods is not carrying on or engaged in a business, trade,\nprofession or occupation in relation to the goods.\nNote:\nThis subsection was inserted as a response to the decision of the High\nCourt of Australia in Wallis v Downard-Pickford (North Queensland)\nPty Ltd [1994] HCA 17.\n\nConsumer protection  Schedule 10\n\nNo. 132, 2018\nTreasury Laws Amendment (Australian Consumer Law Review) Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:treasury-laws-amendment-australian-consumer-law-review-act-2018-sch-9-sec-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0a2b15e140f105e3b05606bf419a54ded1b1f089daa08e0162cea7f5b427f3f0",
      "skos:note": "Avoids doubt about subsection (1)(a) not applying if consignee is not engaged in a business or occupation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/treasury-laws-amendment-australian-consumer-law-review-act-2018#sch-9-sec-2",
